d banning all Chinese students  completely only narrowly deciding  against it after an ambassador pointed  out how it would harm American schools  students and STEM fields in other words  most Chinese students are already  subject to additional scrutiny  the truth is visa issues are not yet  widespread and the US government has at  times even encouraged Chinese arrivals  with trump declaring quote we want to  have Chinese students go to our great  schools and great universities they are  great students and tremendous assets  regardless issues are common enough to  create a perception of risk leading to  an 8% drop of international students in  2018 who increasingly choose other  countries like Canada or affordable  Thailand  the University of Illinois went so far  as to take out a four hundred and twenty  four thousand dollar insurance policy in  case of a significant drop and Chinese  students the US can and should be  worried about Chinese influence on  campuses their free open minded approach  has the potentially dangerous side  effect of also creating a vulnerable  hole easily filled by nationalist  propaganda there has never been a better  time in history to be wary of China's  influence abroad but there has also  never been a more important moment to be  cautious about conflating a government  and its ideology with 1.4 billion  individuals suspecting everyone of  espionage leaves America economically  and culturally weaker not stronger every  year Chinese students contribute 15  billion dollars to the US economy  education is now Australia's third  largest export more than tourism and  behind only iron and coal but whether  economically useful or not cultural  exchanges act as a countervailing force  to propaganda both exposing Chinese  nationals to a wider intellectual world  and American citizens to foreign  cultures the fact that America has so  many high ranking sought after  institutions where even Xi Jinping sends  his daughter is a massive diplomatic  a